IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Part VI of the Interpretation Act 1978 (Northern Territory): Mechanics of legislation, sections 49 to 57B.
-- Reprint as in force at 21 April 2023.
--
-- A function answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE where the text itself says yes or no, and NOTHING where it does not.

§ `Section 49: citation`

DECLARE `Way of citing an Act` IS ONE OF
    `by its short title including the year of enactment`
    `by reference to its number and the calendar year in which it received assent`
    `in a way not named in section 49(1)`

-- An Act may be cited by its short title including the year of enactment, or by its number and the calendar year in which it received assent.
-- src:674 | (1) An Act may be cited in any of the following ways:
-- src:675 | (a) by its short title including the year of enactment;
-- src:676 | (b) by reference to its number and the calendar year in which it received assent.
@ref s 49(1) (src:674-676)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of citing an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(1): the Act may be cited in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `in a way not named in section 49(1)` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Division of an Act by which a provision may be cited` IS ONE OF
    `by its part`
    `by its section`
    `by its subsection`
    `by another division of the Act`
    `not by a division of the Act`

-- A provision may be cited by the part, section, subsection or other division of the Act in which it is contained.
-- src:677 | (2) A provision of an Act may be cited by reference to the part, section, subsection or other division of the Act in which the provision is contained.
@ref s 49(2) (src:677)
GIVEN division IS A `Division of an Act by which a provision may be cited`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(2): the provision may be cited by reference to the division` MEANS
    CONSIDER division
    WHEN `not by a division of the Act` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- A reference mentioned in subsection (2) must be made according to the copy of the Act printed or purporting to be printed by the Government Printer.
-- src:678 | (3) A reference mentioned in subsection (2) must be made according to the copy of the Act printed or purporting to be printed by the Government Printer.
@ref s 49(3) (src:678)
GIVEN `the reference is made according to the copy of the Act printed or purporting to be printed by the Government Printer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 49(3): the reference meets the requirement of subsection (3)` MEANS JUST `the reference is made according to the copy of the Act printed or purporting to be printed by the Government Printer`

§ `Sections 50 to 52: references to other legislation`

DECLARE `Version of other legislation` IS ONE OF
    `the legislation as made`
    `the legislation as amended with effect from`
        HAS `the day on which the latest amendment took effect` IS A DATE

-- The latest of the given days that is on or before the day asked about, if any.
-- src:680 | (1) A reference in an Act to other legislation is a reference to the other legislation as amended from time to time.
@ref s 50(1) (src:680)
GIVEN `the days on which amendments of the other legislation took effect` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Version of other legislation`
`s 50(1): the version of the other legislation that a reference to it is a reference to on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN amendment YIELD Day amendment AT MOST Day `the day asked about`) `the days on which amendments of the other legislation took effect`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the legislation as made`
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `the legislation as amended with effect from`
            (Date (maximum (map (GIVEN amendment YIELD Day amendment) (x FOLLOWED BY rest))))

-- A reference in an amending provision to the other Act is a reference to it as in force immediately before the commencement of the provision.
-- src:681 | (2) If a provision of an Act amends another Act, a reference in the provision to the other Act is a reference to the other Act as in force immediately before the commencement of the provision.
@ref s 50(2) (src:681)
GIVEN `the days on which amendments of the other Act took effect` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day on which the amending provision commences` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Version of other legislation`
`s 50(2): the version of the other Act that the reference in the amending provision is a reference to` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN amendment YIELD Day amendment LESS THAN Day `the day on which the amending provision commences`) `the days on which amendments of the other Act took effect`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the legislation as made`
    WHEN x FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        `the legislation as amended with effect from`
            (Date (maximum (map (GIVEN amendment YIELD Day amendment) (x FOLLOWED BY rest))))

-- A reference to a law or statutory instrument, or a provision of one, includes a reference to the statutory instruments in force under it.
-- src:683 | (1) In an Act, a reference (either generally or specifically) to a law or statutory instrument, or a provision of a law or statutory instrument, includes a reference to the statutory instruments in force under the law, instrument or provision.
@ref s 51(1) (src:683)
GIVEN `the statutory instrument is in force under the law, instrument or provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(1): the reference includes the statutory instrument` MEANS
    IF `the statutory instrument is in force under the law, instrument or provision` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Law within section 51(2)` IS ONE OF
    `an Act of the Commonwealth`
    `an Act of a State`
    `an Act of a Territory`
    `a law of a kind not named in section 51(2)`

-- In section 51, law includes an Act of the Commonwealth or a State or Territory.
-- src:685 | law includes an Act of the Commonwealth or a State or Territory.
@ref s 51(2) (src:685)
GIVEN law IS A `Law within section 51(2)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 51(2): the thing is a law` MEANS
    CONSIDER law
    WHEN `a law of a kind not named in section 51(2)` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Source of an Act that is cited` IS ONE OF
    `an Imperial Act`
    `a Commonwealth Act`
    `an Act of a State`
    `an Act of another Territory of Australia`
    `an Act of some other legislature`

-- An Imperial Act, a Commonwealth Act or an Act of a State or another Territory may be cited by the place by whose Parliament it was passed together with a mode of reference sufficient in Acts passed by that Parliament.
-- src:687 | An Imperial Act, a Commonwealth Act or an Act of a State or another Territory of Australia may be cited by a reference to the place by the Parliament of which the Act was passed together with such mode of reference as is sufficient in Acts passed by that Parliament and, where it is so cited and that Act is subsequently amended, the reference shall, from the date of the amendment, be deemed to be to that Act as so amended.
@ref s 52 (src:687)
GIVEN source IS A `Source of an Act that is cited`
      `the mode of reference is sufficient in Acts passed by that Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52: the Act may be cited by the place of its Parliament together with that mode of reference` MEANS
    CONSIDER source
    WHEN `an Act of some other legislature` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE IF `the mode of reference is sufficient in Acts passed by that Parliament` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Where such an Act is subsequently amended, the reference is, from the date of the amendment, deemed to be to the Act as so amended.
@ref s 52 (src:687)
GIVEN `the day of the amendment` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52: the reference is deemed to be to the Act as amended on the day` MEANS
    JUST (Day `the day asked about` AT LEAST Day `the day of the amendment`)

§ `Section 53: references within an Act to its own provisions`

DECLARE `Unit that a reference names` IS ONE OF
    `referring to a Part`
    `referring to a section`
    `referring to a Schedule`
    `referring to a Division`
    `referring to a subsection`
    `referring to a paragraph`
    `referring to a subparagraph`
    `referring to a form, item or clause`

DECLARE `Place where a reference stands` IS ONE OF
    `anywhere in the Act`
    `in a Part of the Act`
    `in a section of the Act`
    `in a subsection of a section of the Act`
    `in a paragraph of a section, or of a subsection of a section, of the Act`
    `in a Schedule, or part of a Schedule, to the Act`

-- The thing of which the unit named is a part, read from where the reference stands.
-- (1) a Part, section or Schedule: of the Act.  (2) in a Part, a Division: of that Part.  (3) in a section, a subsection or paragraph: of that section.
-- (4) in a subsection, a paragraph: of that subsection.  (5) in a paragraph, a subparagraph: of that paragraph.  (6) in a Schedule or part, a form, item or clause: of that Schedule or part.
-- Subsection (4) is the narrower rule for a paragraph named from inside a subsection; (3) would give the section.
-- src:689 | (1) A reference in an Act to a Part, section or Schedule shall be read as a reference to a Part or section of, or a Schedule to, that Act.
-- src:690 | (2) A reference in a Part of an Act to a Division shall be read as a reference to a Division of that Part.
-- src:691 | (3) A reference in a section of an Act to a subsection or paragraph shall be read as a reference to a subsection or paragraph of that section.
-- src:692 | (4) A reference in a subsection of a section of an Act to a paragraph shall be read as a reference to a paragraph of that subsection.
-- src:693 | (5) A reference in a paragraph of a section, or of a subsection of a section, of an Act to a subparagraph shall be read as a reference to a subparagraph of that paragraph.
-- src:694 | (6) A reference in a Schedule, or part of a Schedule, to an Act to a form, paragraph, item or clause, shall be read as a reference to a form, paragraph, item or clause of that Schedule or part.
@ref s 53(1) to (6) (src:689-694)
GIVEN unit IS A `Unit that a reference names`
      place IS A `Place where a reference stands`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 53(1) to (6): the thing of which the unit that the reference names is a part` MEANS
    CONSIDER unit
    WHEN `referring to a Part` THEN JUST "that Act"
    WHEN `referring to a section` THEN JUST "that Act"
    WHEN `referring to a Schedule` THEN JUST "that Act"
    WHEN `referring to a Division` THEN
        IF place EQUALS `in a Part of the Act` THEN JUST "that Part" ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `referring to a subsection` THEN
        CONSIDER place
        WHEN `in a section of the Act` THEN JUST "that section"
        WHEN `in a subsection of a section of the Act` THEN JUST "that section"
        WHEN `in a paragraph of a section, or of a subsection of a section, of the Act` THEN JUST "that section"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `referring to a paragraph` THEN
        CONSIDER place
        WHEN `in a section of the Act` THEN JUST "that section"
        WHEN `in a subsection of a section of the Act` THEN JUST "that subsection"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHEN `referring to a subparagraph` THEN
        IF place EQUALS `in a paragraph of a section, or of a subsection of a section, of the Act` THEN JUST "that paragraph" ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `referring to a form, item or clause` THEN
        IF place EQUALS `in a Schedule, or part of a Schedule, to the Act` THEN JUST "that Schedule or part" ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Unit named inside a section` IS ONE OF
    `a subsection named inside a section`
    `a paragraph named inside a section`
    `a subparagraph named inside a section`

-- The identifier, as the text prints identifiers, of a subsection, paragraph or subparagraph named from inside a section: for example, paragraph (b) named inside subsection (1) of section 25 is 25(1)(b).
@ref s 53(3), (4), (5) (src:689-693)
GIVEN unit IS A `Unit named inside a section`
      label IS A STRING
      section IS A STRING
      `the subsection in which the reference stands, if any` IS A MAYBE STRING
      `the paragraph in which the reference stands, if any` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 53(3), (4), (5): the identifier of the unit named` MEANS
    CONSIDER unit
    WHEN `a subsection named inside a section` THEN JUST (section APPEND label)
    WHEN `a paragraph named inside a section` THEN
        CONSIDER `the subsection in which the reference stands, if any`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (section APPEND label)
        WHEN JUST subsection THEN JUST ((section APPEND subsection) APPEND label)
    WHEN `a subparagraph named inside a section` THEN
        CONSIDER `the paragraph in which the reference stands, if any`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST paragraph THEN
            CONSIDER `the subsection in which the reference stands, if any`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (((section APPEND paragraph) APPEND label))
            WHEN JUST subsection THEN JUST ((((section APPEND subsection) APPEND paragraph) APPEND label))

-- A reference to a form in an Act whose Schedule, or only one of whose Schedules, contains a form or forms, is read as a reference to a form in that Schedule.
-- src:695 | (7) A reference to a form in an Act the Schedule to which or only one of the Schedules to which contains a form or forms shall be read as a reference to a form in that Schedule.
@ref s 53(7) (src:695)
GIVEN `the Act has one Schedule, or only one of its Schedules contains a form or forms` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 53(7): the reference to a form is read as a reference to a form in that Schedule` MEANS
    IF `the Act has one Schedule, or only one of its Schedules contains a form or forms` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 54 and 55: sections and the material that is part of an Act`

-- Every section of an Act has effect as a substantive enactment without introducing words.
-- src:697 | Every section of an Act shall have effect as a substantive enactment without introducing words.
@ref s 54 (src:697)
GIVEN `the section has introducing words` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54: the section has effect as a substantive enactment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the section has introducing words`
    WHEN TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN FALSE THEN JUST TRUE

DECLARE `Material in or printed with an Act` IS ONE OF
    `a heading to a Chapter, Part, Division or Subdivision`
    `a heading to a section`
        HAS `the day on which the Act was enacted`                       IS A DATE
            `the day on which the heading was amended or inserted, if it was` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `an example or note in the text of an Act`
    `a Schedule to an Act`
    `a marginal note, footnote, endnote or other note that is not part of the text of the Act`
    `other material`

-- (1) a heading to a Chapter, Part, Division or Subdivision is part of the Act.  (2) a heading to a section is part of the Act if the Act was enacted after 1 July 2006 or the heading was amended or inserted after 1 July 2006.
-- (4) an example or note in the text of an Act is part of the provision it relates to.  (5) a Schedule is part of the Act.  (6) a marginal note, footnote, endnote or other note that is not part of the text is not part of the Act.
-- src:699 | (1) A heading to a Chapter, Part, Division or Subdivision of an Act is part of the Act.
-- src:700 | (2) A heading to a section of an Act is part of the Act if:
-- src:701 | (a) the Act is enacted after 1 July 2006; or
-- src:702 | (b) the heading is amended or inserted after 1 July 2006.
-- src:703 | (3) Subsection (2) does not prevent the amendment of a heading to a section by an Act.
-- src:704 | (4) An example or note in the text of an Act is part of the provision of the Act to which it relates.
-- src:705 | (5) A Schedule to an Act is part of the Act.
-- src:706 | (6) A marginal note, footnote, endnote or any other note that is not part of the text of the Act is not part of the Act.
@ref s 55 (src:699-706)
GIVEN material IS A `Material in or printed with an Act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55: the material is part of the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER material
    WHEN `a heading to a Chapter, Part, Division or Subdivision` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a heading to a section` enacted amended THEN
        JUST (Day enacted GREATER THAN Day (Date 1 7 2006)
              OR (CONSIDER amended
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
                  WHEN JUST changed THEN Day changed GREATER THAN Day (Date 1 7 2006)))
    WHEN `an example or note in the text of an Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a Schedule to an Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a marginal note, footnote, endnote or other note that is not part of the text of the Act` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `other material` THEN NOTHING

-- Subsection (2) does not prevent the amendment of a heading to a section by an Act.
-- src:703 | (3) Subsection (2) does not prevent the amendment of a heading to a section by an Act.
@ref s 55(3) (src:703)
GIVEN `the heading is a heading to a section of an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55(3): subsection (2) prevents the amendment of the heading by an Act` MEANS
    IF `the heading is a heading to a section of an Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 56 and 57: numbering`

-- The number of an item among those in a calendar year, in the order of their days: 1 plus the number of those on earlier days in the same year.
-- Two on the same day: the text does not say which is first.
-- src:708 | (1) The Acts which receive assent in each calendar year shall be numbered in regular arithmetical series, beginning with the number one, in the order in which they receive assent.
@ref s 56(1) (src:708)
GIVEN `the days on which the Acts in the calendar year received assent` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day on which the Act received assent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 56(1): the number of the Act` MEANS
    IF   count (filter (GIVEN day YIELD DATE_YEAR day EQUALS DATE_YEAR `the day on which the Act received assent` AND Day day EQUALS Day `the day on which the Act received assent`) `the days on which the Acts in the calendar year received assent`) GREATER THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (1 PLUS count (filter (GIVEN day YIELD DATE_YEAR day EQUALS DATE_YEAR `the day on which the Act received assent` AND Day day LESS THAN Day `the day on which the Act received assent`) `the days on which the Acts in the calendar year received assent`))

-- An Act that receives the Governor-General's assent is deemed to receive assent on the day on which notification of the assent is published in the Gazette.
-- src:709 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), an Act which receives the Governor-General's assent is deemed to receive assent on the day upon which notification that the Governor-General has assented to the Act is published in the Gazette.
@ref s 56(2) (src:709)
GIVEN `the Act received the Governor-General's assent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which notification of the assent is published in the Gazette` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 56(2): the day on which the Act is deemed to receive assent` MEANS
    IF `the Act received the Governor-General's assent` THEN JUST `the day on which notification of the assent is published in the Gazette` ELSE NOTHING

-- Section 57 applies to subordinate legislation other than rules of court relating only to dates of sittings, by-laws of the Commissioner for Public Employment, and legislation that expressly disapplies it.
-- src:711 | (1) This section applies to subordinate legislation other than:
-- src:712 | (a) rules of court that relate only to dates of sittings of a court; or
-- src:713 | (b) by-laws made by the Commissioner for Public Employment under the Public Sector Employment and Management Act 1993; or
-- src:714 | (c) subordinate legislation that expressly provides this section does not apply to it.
@ref s 57(1) (src:711-714)
GIVEN `it is a rule of court that relates only to dates of sittings of a court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a by-law made by the Commissioner for Public Employment under the Public Sector Employment and Management Act 1993` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it expressly provides that section 57 does not apply to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57(1): section 57 applies to the subordinate legislation` MEANS
    JUST (NOT (`it is a rule of court that relates only to dates of sittings of a court`
               OR `it is a by-law made by the Commissioner for Public Employment under the Public Sector Employment and Management Act 1993`
               OR `it expressly provides that section 57 does not apply to it`))

-- Subordinate legislation made in each calendar year is numbered from one, as close as possible to the order in which it is made.
-- src:715 | (2) Subordinate legislation made in each calendar year must be numbered in regular arithmetical series, beginning with the number one, as close as possible to the order in which it is made.
@ref s 57(2) (src:715)
GIVEN `the days on which the subordinate legislation in the calendar year was made` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 57(2): the number of the subordinate legislation` MEANS
    IF   count (filter (GIVEN day YIELD DATE_YEAR day EQUALS DATE_YEAR `the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` AND Day day EQUALS Day `the day on which the subordinate legislation was made`) `the days on which the subordinate legislation in the calendar year was made`) GREATER THAN 1
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (1 PLUS count (filter (GIVEN day YIELD DATE_YEAR day EQUALS DATE_YEAR `the day on which the subordinate legislation was made` AND Day day LESS THAN Day `the day on which the subordinate legislation was made`) `the days on which the subordinate legislation in the calendar year was made`))

-- Subordinate legislation may be cited by the number given to it and the calendar year in which it is made.
-- src:716 | (3) Subordinate legislation may, without prejudice to any other method of citation, be cited by the number given to it and the calendar year in which it is made.
@ref s 57(3) (src:716)
GIVEN `a number has been given to the subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57(3): the subordinate legislation may be cited by its number and the calendar year in which it is made` MEANS
    IF `a number has been given to the subordinate legislation` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 57A and 57B: amendment of instruments and inserted definitions`

-- If a statutory instrument under a parent Act has been amended by an Act, it may be amended, varied, repealed, rescinded or revoked by a statutory instrument under the parent Act.
-- src:718 | (1) If a statutory instrument under an Act (the parent Act) has been amended by an Act, the instrument may be amended, varied, repealed, rescinded or revoked by a statutory instrument under the parent Act.
@ref s 57A(1) (src:718)
GIVEN `the statutory instrument has been amended by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57A(1): the statutory instrument may be amended, varied, repealed, rescinded or revoked by a statutory instrument under the parent Act` MEANS
    IF `the statutory instrument has been amended by an Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- Subsection (1) applies to amendments effected before or after the commencement of the section.
-- src:719 | (2) Subsection (1) applies in relation to amendments effected before or after the commencement of this section.
@ref s 57A(2) (src:719)
GIVEN `the amendment was effected before the commencement of section 57A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 57A(2): subsection (1) applies in relation to the amendment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the amendment was effected before the commencement of section 57A`
    WHEN TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN FALSE THEN JUST TRUE

-- A definition inserted in a provision containing definitions, where the amending Act does not say where, is taken to be inserted in alphabetical order.
-- The text does not say how capital letters or punctuation are ranked; the order in which section 17 prints its own terms is by letters without regard to capitals, so terms are compared with capitals made small and are otherwise compared as given.
-- src:721 | If an Act amends a provision of another Act that contains definitions by inserting another definition in that provision but does not specify where in that provision the definition is to be inserted, it is taken to be inserted in alphabetical order.
@ref s 57B (src:721)
GIVEN `the terms already defined, in the order printed` IS A LIST OF STRING
      `the term inserted` IS A STRING
      `the amending Act specifies where the definition is to be inserted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF STRING)
`s 57B: the terms in the order they stand after the insertion` MEANS
    IF   `the amending Act specifies where the definition is to be inserted`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (append (append (filter (GIVEN known YIELD TOLOWER known LESS THAN TOLOWER `the term inserted`) `the terms already defined, in the order printed`)
                              (LIST `the term inserted`))
                      (filter (GIVEN known YIELD TOLOWER known AT LEAST TOLOWER `the term inserted`) `the terms already defined, in the order printed`))
